{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788465377-mIHKj4WbLfANScV1VNm4","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed: `solara.use_reactive(value)` returns the passed reactive as-is when given a `solara.Reactive` (line 126-127). So calling `model_parameters = solara.use_reactive(model_parameters)` unconditionally works for both:\n- A reactive passed in (SolaraViz case) → returned as-is\n- A plain dict or None → new reactive wrapping `{}` or the dict\n\nNow let me apply the changes. I'll make the three source changes and update the test file to match upstream.\n\nPlan:\n1. `ModelController`: replace conditional `use_reactive({})` with unconditional initialization.\n2. `ModelCreator`: same.\n3. `_check_model_params`: add `name != \"kwargs\"` and `\"kwargs\" not in model_parameters`.\n4. `tests/test_solara_viz.py`: add `ModelWithKwargs` tests (matching upstream).\n5. Run tests and verify the conditional-hook warnings are gone.\n\nLet me create a task list? This is a fairly contained change — 4 edits + verification. I'll skip heavy task tracking; it's a simple, short task. Actually the reminders keep nudging; but guidance says only use if relevant. It's a small task with ~3 edits. I'll proceed directly.\n\nLet me make the edits.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Parasail","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9281beb7-8454-46da-9c7e-88efbd79f1a1","uuid":"c69075e8-d9be-4af6-ac61-07ddf2508dc2","timestamp":"2026-09-03T19:56:20.882Z","request_id":"gen-1788465377-mIHKj4WbLfANScV1VNm4"}
