y, with retries? solara/tasks.py:1009 — the task failure might occur in an effect, asynchronously after mount. In the passing test, the effect error might be swallowed by reacton (errors in effects logged, not raised).\n\nIn my failing test, the error was raised at line 114 — the `solara.render(Harness(), handle_error=False)` call. So with handle_error=False, the use_task error is re-raised; with default handle_error=True it's swallowed. The repo's test_call_space_drawer renders SolaraViz (which contains ModelController with use_task) with default handling and the matplotlib mock IS called — meaning the use_task error did NOT abort the entire render in that path?\n\nHmm, actually wait. Let me reconsider: maybe the use_task error only happens on the SECOND render pass (my Harness renders two components; solara.render does an initial render + forces rerenders?). Or the difference: `solara.render(SolaraViz(...))` in the repo test vs my `solara.render(Harness(), handle_error=False)`.\n\nLet me just empirically test: render SolaraViz with explicit components and handle_error=False, and see if it raises the event-loop error.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Parasail","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9281beb7-8454-46da-9c7e-88efbd79f1a1","uuid":"3c224139-c744-4fe0-936a-df592635992b","timestamp":"2026-09-03T19:58:29.670Z","request_id":"gen-1788465498-OmlPuMvtRON2xYjhh6k8"}
