{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788465513-6MG9NY1OECMJ6GAm6KCx","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting — `SolaraViz` with explicit components renders fine with `handle_error=False`, and there are **zero conditional-hook warnings**. So the use_task event-loop issue in my ModelController harness test was specific to how I rendered it (perhaps the `▶`/play task only triggers in certain conditions, or SolaraViz's order of rendering matters). Whatever — the important verification: full SolaraViz renders cleanly with no conditional-hook warnings, using explicit components (the default-components path has a pre-existing bug at this commit, unrelated).\n\nNow let me finalize the verification: I'll adapt the harness tests:\n1. SolaraViz renders with `**kwargs` models across all four model_params variants (None, {}, dict, Slider) — no conditional warnings.\n2. ModelCreator with shared reactive / plain dict / None — parameter tracking initialized correctly.\n3. Button-level step/reset — I can test via SolaraViz's rendered buttons if use_task doesn't break... The earlier ModelController-only harness failed at render. Let me test the step/reset buttons through full SolaraViz render instead.","signature":""}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Parasail","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9281beb7-8454-46da-9c7e-88efbd79f1a1","uuid":"54ac9031-3966-4b2e-b411-ab3184fb9bb6","timestamp":"2026-09-03T19:58:49.733Z","request_id":"gen-1788465513-6MG9NY1OECMJ6GAm6KCx"}
