t. Let me instead search the full widget tree — `rc.find` searches from the root. Since sidebar is rendered elsewhere (it's a special layout), let me check `rc.find(vw.Btn)` works... The failure shows the root contains Sheet > Html, Html, GridLayout > Image — that's just the main content (the mpl space component image). So sidebar content is NOT part of this render context root.\n\nTo verify buttons, I can use `solara.render` differently or find the sidebar widgets. Let me check reacton's render context — maybe there's `rc.find(vw.Btn, recursive=True)` — no, find is recursive by default within the tree. The sidebar content is registered in a separate root.\n\nFor the repo's own test approach, they use mocker.spy and check calls rather than widget interactions. Let me verify the button interactions differently: get all rendered widgets via the render context... Hmm.\n\nAlternative: use `solara.render` on a harness that renders ModelController content inside the main body (not sidebar). But the earlier ModelController-only harness failed with the event-loop error at render. Let me investigate that more: maybe use_task only fails when the render happens without a running loop, and in SolaraViz it worked... Because in SolaraViz, ModelController is rendered inside `solara.Sidebar()` context. Interesting — maybe sidebar rendering defers.\n\nLet me simplify: for the button test, render ModelController inside a Sidebar within my harness, mirroring SolaraViz's structure. Or, simpler: drop the interactive button tests from my verification harness and instead directly verify the semantics that changed:\n\n1. Conditional-hook warnings gone when rendering SolaraViz (done — 0 warnings across all four model_params variants).\n2. Parameter tracking with/without initial params (section (a) done; section (b) — check reactive value via a callback instead of finding the slider).\n3. `_check_model_params` semantics (done).\n4. Step/reset: the do_reset/do_step code paths are unchanged by