{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788465654-IpVPP1entG9bEGuuqqBd","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bebf93b95749dced","caller":{"type":"direct"},"name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/logs/agent/sessions/projects/-testbed/memory/solara-test-renderer-sidebar.md","content":"---\nname: solara-test-renderer-sidebar\ndescription: In mesa's testbed, solara.render() omits solara.Sidebar content from the returned widget tree, and use_task needs a running event loop\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nWhen testing mesa's Solara visualization components (`mesa/visualization/solara_viz.py`) with `solara.render()`:\n\n- Content rendered inside `solara.Sidebar()` (e.g. `ModelController` buttons, `ModelCreator` sliders) does NOT appear in the returned render context's widget tree — `rc.find(vw.Btn)` / `rc.find(vw.Slider)` find nothing. To test those widgets, render the component in the main body of a harness component instead.\n- `ModelController` uses `solara.lab.use_task`, which raises `RuntimeError: no running event loop` when rendered without one. Wrap the render call inside `asyncio.run(async def ...)` (render in the loop's thread — `run_in_executor` does not work).\n- `solara.lab.use_task`-based renders fail with `handle_error=False` outside a loop; repo tests like `test_call_space_drawer` pass only because default `handle_error=True` swallows the error.\n- Solara's hook validation emits `UserWarning: ... use_reactive found within a conditional` (SH102) for hooks called under `if` in components; warnings can be captured with `warnings.catch_warnings(record=True)` and filtering on \"conditional\"/\"rules of hooks\".\n\n**Why:** These behaviors silently hide UI from test assertions and cost significant debugging time.\n**How to apply:** Assert on sidebar widgets via a main-body harness; run renders needing `use_task` inside `asyncio.run`.\n"}}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Parasail","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9281beb7-8454-46da-9c7e-88efbd79f1a1","uuid":"9567e612-59e5-4daa-928f-18a9dd3dd296","timestamp":"2026-09-03T20:01:01.701Z","request_id":"gen-1788465654-IpVPP1entG9bEGuuqqBd"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bebf93b95749dced","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /logs/agent/sessions/projects/-testbed/memory/solara-test-renderer-sidebar.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9281beb7-8454-46da-9c7e-88efbd79f1a1","uuid":"642316d8-6594-4566-ac29-f6dec9540467","timestamp":"2026-09-03T20:01:01.710Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/logs/agent/sessions/projects/-testbed/memory/solara-test-renderer-sidebar.md","content":"---\nname: solara-test-renderer-sidebar\ndescription: \"In mesa's testbed, solara.render() omits solara.Sidebar content from the returned widget tree, and use_task needs a running event loop\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 9281beb7-8454-46da-9c7e-88efbd79f1a1\n  modified: 2026-09-03T20:01:01.707Z\n---\n\nWhen testing mesa's Solara visualization components (`mesa/visualization/solara_viz.py`) with `solara.render()`:\n\n- Content rendered inside `solara.Sidebar()` (e.g. `ModelController` buttons, `ModelCreator` sliders) does NOT appear in the returned render context's widget tree — `rc.find(vw.Btn)` / `rc.find(vw.Slider)` find nothing. To test those widgets, render the component in the main body of a harness component instead.\n- `ModelController` uses `solara.lab.use_task`, which raises `RuntimeError: no running event loop` when rendered without one. Wrap the render call inside `asyncio.run(async def ...)` (render in the loop's thread — `run_in_executor` does not work).\n- `solara.lab.use_task`-based renders fail with `handle_error=False` outside a loop; repo tests like `test_call_space_drawer` pass only because default `handle_error=True` swallows the error.\n- Solara's hook validation emits `UserWarning: ... use_reactive found within a conditional` (SH102) for hooks called under `if` in components; warnings can be captured with `warnings.catch_warnings(record=True)` and filtering on \"conditional\"/\"rules of hooks\".\n\n**Why:** These behaviors silently hide UI from test assertions and cost significant debugging time.\n**How to apply:** Assert on sidebar widgets via a main-body harness; run renders needing `use_task` inside `asyncio.run`.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false,"memdirStamped":true}}
